# tilc.til - a TIL compiler written in TIL ("TIL Core" subset, see selfhost/README.md)
#
#   til run --vm selfhost/tilc.til input.til output.tbc
#   til build --target vm selfhost/tilc.til -o tilc.tbc
#   tilvm tilc.tbc input.til output.tbc          (any TIL VM, e.g. a calculator)
#
# Produces .tbc bytecode v2 with the same runtime behaviour as `til build
# --target vm` (src/til.py). The structure mirrors the Python front end
# (Lexer, Parser, BytecodeCompiler, TBCModule.to_bytes) so that both accept
# the same syntax and emit the same instructions and line tables.
#
# Memory: tokens are streamed (only a small look-ahead window is kept); the
# first pass parses the whole file but keeps only declarations; the second
# pass re-lexes each function body from its saved source position, compiles
# it and keeps just its bytecode (a string). The output is built from string
# chunks. Integers are handled as 16-bit limbs so the compiler gives the same
# result on 32-bit and 64-bit VMs; float literals are converted to IEEE 754
# bits exactly with integer arithmetic (no host floats are used).

